course: dictionary
lesson: 7114
title: Pedestrian: a person on foot
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pedestrian is a person who is walking, not riding a bike or driving a car. You are a pedestrian each time you walk to school along the pavement. Pedestrian can be a noun (a pedestrian) or an adjective (pedestrian crossing).
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «Pedestrian crossing» tells you it is a place for people on foot to cross the road. «Drivers must give way to pedestrians» tells you drivers must stop and wait for people who are walking.
explain: Pedestrian can also mean dull and ordinary, with nothing special. Context shows you which meaning to use. If the sentence is about roads or walking, it is the first meaning. If it is about a dull film or a plain meal, it means ordinary. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A pedestrian is a person who is walking, not riding or driving.
fact: A pedestrian crossing is a place where people on foot can cross the road.
fact: «Pedestrian» can also be an adjective meaning dull and ordinary, with nothing special.
fact: «Some crows in Japan drop nuts at pedestrian crossings for cars to crack.»
fact: «A no pedestrians sign means nobody may walk there.»
exercise: What is a pedestrian? | A driver in a car | A cyclist on a bike path | A bus passenger | *A person who is walking
exercise: «A no pedestrians sign means nobody may walk there.» What does this sign tell you? | Everyone must walk very slowly | *Nobody may walk there | Only bikes may use this road
exercise: Jo says, «The film was pedestrian, nothing special at all.» What does pedestrian mean here? | Very fast and exciting | Brightly coloured | Full of people walking | *Dull and ordinary
test: «At a pedestrian crossing a red standing figure means wait, even if the road looks empty.» Why must you wait? | The road is always closed to cars | *The cars may have a green light and come fast | The crossing is broken and cannot be used
test: Which person is a pedestrian? | Driver of a white van | Man riding a bicycle | *Girl walking to school with her mum | Boy on a scooter
exam: In «The meal was pedestrian», what kind of word is pedestrian? | Verb | Noun | *Adjective | Adverb
